Changes with nginx 1.29.5                                        15 Jun 2026

    *) Feature: HTTP response status codes are now managed through a
       centralized, registry-backed API. The ngx_http_status_set() function
       is the single point that assigns a response status, and the
       ngx_http_status_reason(), ngx_http_status_validate(),
       ngx_http_status_register(), and ngx_http_status_is_cacheable()
       functions provide reason phrases, RFC 9110 metadata, a registration
       seam, and cacheability information.

    *) Feature: optional RFC 9110 section 15 status code validation, enabled
       with the "--with-http_status_validation" configure option; validation
       is disabled by default and adds no overhead when not enabled.

    *) Change: the duplicated status reason-phrase and error-page lookup
       tables have been consolidated onto the new status registry, and the
       divergent NGX_HTTP_LAST_2XX and NGX_HTTP_OFF_* offset macros have
       been removed; status lines and error-page bodies remain
       byte-identical to previous releases, and the nginx-specific status
       codes 444 and 494-499 are preserved.
